module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanYM4SU2PrincipalLogDexpBridgeExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROW A1a, THE SAME-OBJECT STEP:
--   THE REPOSITORY'S PRINCIPAL-LOG FRECHET DERIVATIVE *IS*
--   I - (1/2) ad_Y + c ad_Y^2
--
-- PRIMARY SOURCES
--
-- Brian C. Hall, "Lie Groups, Lie Algebras, and Representations: An
-- Elementary Introduction", second edition, Springer (2015).
-- DOI: 10.1007/978-3-319-13467-3.
--
-- Tadeusz Balaban, "Renormalization Group Approach to Lattice Gauge Field
-- Theories. I.", Communications in Mathematical Physics 109 (1987), 249--301.
-- DOI: 10.1007/BF01215223.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE CLOSES.
--
-- Two representations of the same operator live in this tree:
--
--   (i)  `BalabanCMP109SU2PrincipalLogJacobianStructureExact` writes the
--        inverse-dexp operator in axis/plane form,
--
--            J v  =  a v  +  (1 - a) <n,v> n  +  sigma (n x v) ,
--
--        with n the logarithm axis and a the (still analytic) radial
--        coefficient;
--
--   (ii) `BalabanYM4SU2DexpJacobianDeterminantExact` computes determinants of
--        the Cayley-Hamilton span  I + alpha ad_Y + beta ad_Y^2 , and needs to
--        know that the chart differential *is* the span element with
--        alpha = -1/2, beta = c.
--
-- The bridge between (i) and (ii) was the missing same-chart part of the Haar
-- statement.  It is supplied here as an exact identity of 3x3 rational
-- matrices: writing Y = s n with n a unit axis,
--
--     dexp_Y^{-1}  =  I - (1/2) ad_Y + c ad_Y^2
--                  =  structureMatrix a sigma n ,
--     a = 1 - 4 s^2 c ,      sigma = - s .
--
-- (`dexpInverseIsPrincipalLogOperator`; the vector form is
-- `dexpInverseActsAsPrincipalLog`.)  In particular the two representations
-- have the *same* radial coefficient, so the repository's analytic input
--
--     a = s cot s        (cleared:  S a = s C,  S = sin s, C = cos s)
--
-- is literally the removable-singularity input of the determinant module,
--
--     S (1 - 4 s^2 c) = s C ,     i.e.    c = (1 - s cot s) / (4 s^2) .
--
-- Feeding that through the determinant theorem gives, with no further Haar
-- algebra,
--
--     det dexp_Y^{-1} = (s / sin s)^2 ,     J(Y) = (sin s / s)^2
--
-- in cleared form  J s^2 = (sin s)^2  (`haarDensityFromPrincipalLogChart`).
--
-- WHAT IS *NOT* PROVED HERE.  The real-analytic value of the radial
-- coefficient a = s cot s itself: it enters, as everywhere in this tree, as
-- the cleared scalar relation  S a = s C, and is supplied by the Bishop-real
-- enclosures.  What is proved is that the *operator* identification needs no
-- new Lie theory: it is the displayed polynomial identity.  Row A stays open;
-- the frozen research count stays at 4.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt.  Checked with
-- `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

